      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.645,
            0.047,
            0.848,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "A Peek Beyond the Point"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.088,
            0.575,
            0.124
          ],
          "content": "equal to 6 units and 3 one-tenths, i.e., $6   { \\frac { 3 } { 1 0 } } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.138,
            0.847,
            0.178
          ],
          "content": "？ The lengths of the body parts of a honeybee are given. Find its total length."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.187,
            0.32,
            0.221
          ],
          "content": "Head: $2   \\frac { 3 } { 1 0 }$ units"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.22,
            0.337,
            0.251
          ],
          "content": "Thorax: $5 { \\frac { 4 } { 1 0 } }$ units"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.25,
            0.362,
            0.282
          ],
          "content": "Abdomen: $7 \\frac { 5 } { 1 0 }$ units"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.617,
            0.172,
            0.821,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": "Head <u>Thorax</u> abdomen"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.587,
            0.173,
            0.836,
            0.304
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.29,
            0.571,
            0.325
          ],
          "content": "The length of Shylaja’s hand is $1 2   \\frac { 4 } { 1 0 }$ units,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.321,
            0.848,
            0.355
          ],
          "content": "and her palm is $6 { \\frac { 7 } { 1 0 } }$ units, as shown in the picture. What is the length"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.358,
            0.456,
            0.379
          ],
          "content": "of the longest (middle) finger?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.397,
            0.575,
            0.476
          ],
          "content": "The length of the finger can be found by evaluating $\\left( 1 2 + { \\cfrac { 4 } { 1 0 } } \\right) - \\left( 6 + { \\cfrac { 7 } { 1 0 } } \\right)$ . This can be done in different ways. For example,"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.58,
            0.448,
            0.678,
            0.479
          ],
          "content": "12 10 4 units"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.672,
            0.363,
            0.937,
            0.538
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.854,
            0.453,
            0.939,
            0.486
          ],
          "content": "7 6 10 units"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.184,
            0.492,
            0.429,
            0.731
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned} (a)  \\quad & 12 + \\frac{4}{10} - 6 - \\frac{7}{10} \\\\& = (12 - 6) + \\left( \\frac{4}{10} - \\frac{7}{10} \\right) \\\\& = 6 - \\frac{3}{10} \\\\& = 5 + 1 - \\frac{3}{10} \\\\& = 5 + \\frac{10}{10} - \\frac{3}{10} \\\\& = 5 + \\frac{7}{10} = 5 \\frac{7}{10}\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.486,
            0.607,
            0.613,
            0.652
          ],
          "content": "Discuss what is being done here and why."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.747,
            0.474,
            0.869
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{array}{ccc}( b ) & 12\\dfrac{4}{10} &  \\\\\\underbrace{-6\\dfrac{7}{10}} & \\longrightarrow & 11\\dfrac{14}{10} \\\\&  & -6\\dfrac{7}{10} \\\\&  & =5\\dfrac{7}{10} \\\\\\end{array}",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.879,
            0.849,
            0.917
          ],
          "content": "As in the case of counting numbers, it is convenient to start subtraction from the tenths. We cannot remove 7 one-tenths from 4"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.812,
            0.939,
            0.839,
            0.955
          ],
          "content": "51"
        }
      ]
    }
